From 1e1b42777a7fad98ef62f01fa9ed7672d05c988c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:38:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Verify source registry TLS by default; make skipping it
 an explicit option

Every mirror operation ran oc-mirror with --src-tls-verify=false and
--dest-tls-verify=false hardcoded, so certificates of the source
registries (normally registry.redhat.io, often through an enterprise
proxy) were never checked.

Drop both flags. TLS of the source registries is now verified unless
the user turns on the new per-operation optional flag
skipSourceTlsVerify (UI switch "Skip TLS verification for source
registries", with a warning), which adds --src-tls-verify=false. The
destination is always a local file:// directory, so there is no
destination TLS setting to keep.

Tests: default run passes no tls-verify flags; the opt-in passes
--src-tls-verify=false before the mirror URL; false keeps verification;
a non-boolean is rejected. The first three fail on the previous code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
